{0 ocgtk index}

The {b ocgtk} package provides OCaml bindings to GTK4 and its supporting
libraries. Each namespace below is a separate sub-library; the
[.generated_stubs*] libraries (pure C stubs with no OCaml modules, used
internally to link the generated bindings) are omitted from this index.

{1 Libraries}

{2 {!Ocgtk} }
The top-level module: re-exports every namespace below as a sub-module
(e.g. [Ocgtk.Gtk.Widget]), plus {!Ocglib} as [Ocgtk.Common].

{2 {!Ocgtk_cairo} }
2D vector graphics: drawing contexts, paths, patterns and surfaces.

{2 {!Ocgtk_gdk} }
Low-level windowing, displays, input and events that Gtk is built on.

{2 {!Ocgtk_gdkpixbuf} }
Image loading, scaling and pixel-buffer manipulation.

{2 {!Ocgtk_gio} }
I/O, files, and the application/networking abstractions from GLib's
application framework.

{2 {!Ocgtk_graphene} }
Lightweight 3D transform and geometry types (vectors, matrices, rectangles)
used by Gsk and Gtk.

{2 {!Ocgtk_gsk} }
The GTK scene graph: render nodes and transforms for drawing widgets.

{2 {!Ocgtk_gtk} }
The widget toolkit: windows, widgets, layout and the application model.

{2 {!Ocgtk_pango} }
Text layout and internationalized font rendering.

{2 {!Ocgtk_pangocairo} }
Glue between Pango text layout and Cairo rendering.

{1 GLib and GObject (ocglib)}

The hand-written GLib and GObject modules shared by every library above
are in the separate {b ocglib} package, as {!Ocglib}.
